  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{a}}=3 \\hat{i}-\\hat{j}+2 \\hat{k}, \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{~b}}=\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{a}} \\times(\\hat{i}-2 \\hat{k})$ and $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{c}}=\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{b}} \\times \\hat{k}$. Then the projection of $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{c}}-2 \\hat{j}$ on $\\vec{a}$ is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "F5H7i",
      "text": "$2 \\sqrt{14}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "64SEf",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{14}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ujGRo",
      "text": "$3 \\sqrt{7}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "rQtGn",
      "text": "$2 \\sqrt{7}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{b}}=\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{a}} \\times(\\hat{\\mathrm{i}}-3 \\hat{\\mathrm{k}}) \\\\\n& =\\left|\\begin{array}{ccc}\n\\hat{\\mathrm{i}} & \\hat{\\mathrm{j}} & \\hat{\\mathrm{k}} \\\\\n3 & -1 & 2 \\\\\n1 & 0 & -2\n\\end{array}\\right|=2 \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}+8 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}+\\hat{\\mathrm{k}} \\\\\n& \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{c}}=\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{b}} \\times \\hat{\\mathrm{k}}=8 \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}-2 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}} \\\\\n& \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{c}}-2 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}=8 \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}-4 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}\n\\end{aligned}$\n\nProjection of $(\\hat{\\mathrm{i}}-2 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}})$ on $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{a}}$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& (\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{c}}-2 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}) \\cdot \\hat{\\mathrm{a}}=\\frac{\\langle 8,-4,0\\rangle \\cdot\\langle 3,-1,2\\rangle}{\\sqrt{14}} \\\\\n& =\\frac{28}{\\sqrt{14}}=2 \\sqrt{14}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
